# Build output
/target/
**/target/
**/node_modules/
*.wasm.map
# The `/web/` entries that stood here are gone with the browser client
# (operator, 2026-08-06) — `web/` is not in the tree and is not coming back.
# `wasm32-unknown-unknown` is still built, but only as `test_parity_wasm`'s
# second target under `target/`, so it needs no rule of its own.

# Cargo.lock IS committed — ashfall ships binaries, not a library.

# Local config and state. shard.toml is per-deployment: every knob in the docs
# reads from it, so it is exactly the file that must not be shared.
shard.toml
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Dev certs (ECDSA P-256, regenerated on build per NETCODE §2.2) and any key
# material that wanders in. This repo is PUBLIC.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
certs/

# Runtime artifacts: WAL, snapshots, ledger exports, replays
/data/
*.wal
*.snapshot
anomaly.log

# Editors / OS
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# python bytecode (reference/rip-hooks.py)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Fetched texture candidates: 188 files, ~1.3 GB of other people's pristine
# source images, pulled by assets/textures/fetch_gates_texture_candidates.py.
# The QUEUE is committed (CANDIDATES.md + the csv/xlsx beside it); the pixels
# are not — they are re-fetchable from the URLs in the csv, and a selected one
# earns its place in the tree only after it is measured, packed and recorded in
# MANIFEST.md with its licence. This rule lived in `.git/info/exclude`, which is
# per-clone and uncommitted, so a second clone saw 1.3 GB of untracked files
# with nothing warning it off.
assets/textures/candidates/

# Vendor deliveries under review: `assets/models/To Examine/` is where a
# generated character or animation set lands before it is imported, and it is
# ~600 MB of zips and 28 MB GLBs — the same class as the texture candidates
# above, and kept out for the same two reasons. It is re-downloadable from the
# vendor, and what earns a place in the tree is the IMPORTED file plus its row
# in `assets/models/MANIFEST.md`. `ci/depot.py` already stages from
# `git ls-files` rather than walking, so this is not what stops it shipping —
# it is what stops a second clone finding 600 MB of untracked files with
# nothing warning it off (`CLAUDE.md`'s packager trap says why that rule lived
# in the wrong place once already).
assets/models/To Examine/

# Agent worktrees the harness parks under .claude/ while parallel lanes run.
# Each is a whole duplicate checkout; they are transient and auto-cleaned, and
# committing one would be the depot-walk trap one directory up from where it
# was paid for. Scoped: .claude/skills/ is tracked and ships.
.claude/worktrees/
